{"id":"02ef4680-46a9-45ad-87ba-9d38526af8a3","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a20ab411bf9b4e1e","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/build/capabilities.ts","baseline":{"blob":"4a20a67d586b8cbaade23b58ae6be1e4c2b9f521","start":0,"end":42},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Logger",",","Plugin","}","from","\"","vite","\""]},"context":{"after":"afed7145b7311ebb"}},"payload":{"text":"The capabilities extension's build (extensions/capabilities/): its folder's tsserver plugin, as the package tsserver loads\n(node_modules/capabilities-ts-plugin/), and what that plugin runs: the engine (util/silo's reading of TypeScript's tree) and\nthe canary (tsval's sandboxed background run). Both run inside the plugin, so neither bundles a TypeScript. And the\ndependency baseline's package worker (packages-worker.ts), which the extension starts for a sync.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:08:37.935Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:08:37.935Z"}
{"id":"6078d16d-9f84-4e95-868d-aff024456427","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"3620d7e138cb708d","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/build/capabilities.ts","baseline":{"blob":"1c5713853ef18ed61837964f9e3db3397fa4824b","start":3509,"end":3940},"shape":{"type":"AwaitExpression","atoms":["await","buildPackage","(","root",",","{","\"","customLogger","\"",":","logger",",","\"","base","\"",":","\"","./","\"",",","\"","build","\"",":","{","...","shared",",","\"","modulePreload","\"",":","false",",","\"","rollupOptions","\"",":","{","\"","preserveEntrySignatures","\"",":","\"","strict","\"",",","\"","input","\"",":","{","\"","lsp/packages-worker","\"",":","resolvePath","(","\"","../extensions/capabilities/packages-worker.ts","\"",")","}",",","\"","output","\"",":","{","\"","banner","\"",":","banner",",","\"","chunkFileNames","\"",":","\"","lsp/packages-worker-[name]-[hash].js","\"",",","\"","assetFileNames","\"",":","\"","lsp/packages-worker-[name]-[hash][extname]","\"","}","}","}","}",")"]},"context":{"before":"522342d4ddc09bb9"}},"payload":{"text":"The baseline's package worker (dist/lsp/packages-worker.js): what each dependency's tarball says it can do, and the\njoins (rolldown's browser build, loaded on the first slice). A build of its own: it reads util (and util's env, which\nreads `process` as it loads), so every chunk carries the shim; shared with another worker, a chunk of util would load\nbefore the shim on either's entry. (A worker: no `document` for the preload helper.)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:08:35.231Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:08:35.231Z"}
